;;; A query's `:goal` over a relation the program names nowhere else loads, and
;;; has no row —
;;; M1f **W78**, register row `W78/goal-no-such-relation`, filed by S1f.7.11 (T1f.7.11.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, of whom Ann has paid, and no candidate. The goal asks `(payed
;;; ?g)`, where the program's relation is `paid`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; No declaration, fact, rule or hrule of the program names `payed`, so no state
;;; holds a fact of it and the goal can have no row: refused at load, at the
;;; pattern, one line, on every command (exit 1, `ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `73a0c17d`, release: the program loads, and every state reports *the goal has no
;;; row: undetermined here*, exit 0 on every command, as a goal over `paid` does
;;; in a state that holds no `paid` fact.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.11 (T1f.7.11.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(paid Ann)
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (payed ?g))
